`[0 : v₂]`, the chart centre of `σ₀`, maps to `−|v₂|² i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_pol_v1_axis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_pol_v1_axis","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L235-L238","doc":"The line `[v₁ : 0]`, the chart centre of `σ₁`, maps to `+|v₁|² i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_circular_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_circular_minus","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L214-L216","doc":"Circular polarization `[1 : −i]` goes to `+2 j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_circular_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_circular_plus","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L210-L212","doc":"Circular polarization `[1 : i]` goes to `−2 j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_re","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L207-L208","doc":"The Hopf image is always pure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_real_imJ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_real_imJ","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L202-L205","doc":"**Real (linear) polarizations have Hopf image orthogonal to `j`**: they fill the\n`i`–`k` great circle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.pol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.pol","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L199-L200","doc":"The cone vector of the polarization line `[a + b i : c + d i]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_pair_swap_is_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_pair_swap_is_flip","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L179-L192","doc":"**Swapping the two photons is the global flip** `Γ ↦ −Γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_pair_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_pair_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L160-L177","doc":"**An orthogonal pair of unit photons, read through `Γ_{hopf p₁}`**: `p₁` is\nleft-handed and `p₂` right-handed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_orth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_orth","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L146-L158","doc":"**A Hermitian-orthogonal partner has the antipodal Hopf image**: if the `ℂ`-part of\n`p̄₁ p₂` vanishes and `p₁` is a unit, `hopf p₂ = −|p₂|² hopf p₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_conj_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.orth_conj_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L141-L144","doc":"For `w = c j + d k`, `w i w̄ = −(c² + d²) i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.orthW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.orthW","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L138-L139","doc":"A quaternion `c j + d k`, orthogonal to the complex line `ℂ = ℝ + ℝ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_eq_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_eq_ray","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L107-L136","doc":"**Two unit vectors with the same Hopf image span the same complex line**:\n`w = p̄ p'` is complex (`imJ = imK = 0`) and `p' = p w`, when `2` is cancellable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_eigen_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_eigen_line","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L96-L105","doc":"**The whole complex line through a unit `p` is left-handed for `Γ_{hopf p}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.mul_star_self_of_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.mul_star_self_of_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L92-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.star_mul_self_of_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.star_mul_self_of_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_leftMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_leftMul","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L84-L86","doc":"**Equivariance**: a left multiplication moves the Hopf image by conjugation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_mul_cplx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_mul_cplx","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**The Hopf image is constant on Reeb fibres**: `hopf (p λ) = |λ|² · hopf p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx_conj_unitI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx_conj_unitI","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L73-L76","doc":"`λ i λ̄ = |λ|² i` for complex `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf_mul","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L68-L71","doc":"`hopf (p w) = p (w i w̄) p̄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx_mul_unitI_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx_mul_unitI_comm","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.cplx","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L62-L63","doc":"A complex scalar `a + b i`, the Reeb fibre direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.hopf","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ChiralityPolarizationHopf.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The Hopf map on the model cone: `p ↦ p i p̄`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}